#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/deriving-traits.md:6
msgid "Deriving Traits"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/deriving-traits.md:9
msgid "// Copyright 2025 Google LLC\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/deriving-traits.md:10
msgid "// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/deriving-traits.md:24
msgid ""
"Many traits, protocols, interfaces, have trivial implementations that would "
"be easy to mechanically write."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/deriving-traits.md:27
msgid ""
"Definitions of types (their syntax trees) can be fed to procedural macros "
"(compiler plugins) to automatically generate implementations of traits."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/deriving-traits.md:30
msgid ""
"These macros have to be authored by someone, the compiler cannot figure out "
"everything by itself."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/deriving-traits.md:33
msgid ""
"Many traits have a naive, obvious implementation. Mostly implementations "
"that depend on all fields or variants already implementing the trait."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/deriving-traits.md:36
msgid ""
"`PartialEq`/`Eq` can be derived on types whose fields / variants all "
"implement those traits fairly easily: line up the fields / variants, if any "
"of them don't match then the equality check returns false."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/deriving-traits.md:40
msgid ""
"Derives let us avoid boilerplate mechanically and predictably, the authors "
"of a derive implementation likely authored the trait the derive was "
"implemented with the proper semantics of a trait in mind."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/deriving-traits.md:44
msgid ""
"Ask the class: Have the students had to deal with a codebase where most of "
"the code was trivial boilerplate?"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/deriving-traits.md:47
msgid "This is similar to Haskell's `deriving` system."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/deriving-traits.md:49
msgid "references:"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/refresher/deriving-traits.md:51
msgid ""
"https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/attributes/derive.html#r-attributes."
"derive"
msgstr ""
